## Bare-metal `llama-server` bundle (Linux x86_64, CUDA 13, sm_86)

Self-contained: the CUDA 13 runtime libs are bundled; the host only needs the
**NVIDIA kernel driver**. No Docker required. All image features are built via
the same `cmake-flags.sh`; the web panel is omitted.

### Features
- Speculative decode: `--spec-type draft-dflash,draft-mtp`
- Multi-GPU: `--split-mode {none,layer,row,tensor}`
- `--n-cpu-moe N` (MoE expert offload)
- Model swap (router mode): `--models-dir` + `--models-preset` (INI, Modelfile-like)
- KV-cache quant: `-ctk`/`-ctv` (FA covers quants via `GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON`)
- Auth: `LLAMA_API_KEY` (or `--api-key` / `--api-key-file`)
- `--jinja` (on) + `--tools`
- `--sleep-idle-seconds N`
- HF: `-hf owner/repo:quant`, `LLAMA_CACHE`, `HF_TOKEN`

### Install
```bash
set -e
curl -fL -o llama-bundle.tar.zst \
  https://github.com/OWNER-REPO/releases/download/RELEASE-TAG/ASSET-NAME
curl -fL -o llama-bundle.tar.zst.sha256 \
  https://github.com/OWNER-REPO/releases/download/RELEASE-TAG/ASSET-NAME.sha256
sha256sum -c llama-bundle.tar.zst.sha256
sudo mkdir -p /opt/llama
sudo tar -C /opt/llama --zstd -xf llama-bundle.tar.zst
/opt/llama/llama-server-run doctor
```

### Run
```bash
# single model
/opt/llama/llama-server-run -hf owner/model:Q4_K_M \
  --n-gpu-layers 99 --split-mode layer --spec-type draft-dflash \
  -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 -fa on --api-key your-api-key

# or multi-model router (model swap)
cp /opt/llama/preset.example.ini /etc/llama/presets.ini
/opt/llama/llama-server-run --models-preset /etc/llama/presets.ini --models-max 1
```

### Self-update
```bash
/opt/llama/update.sh
/opt/llama/update.sh --check
/opt/llama/update.sh --dry-run
```

